{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcH6auRYKfJLMvGxB9je", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Did production change since the freeze?** I found no sign that it did, but I can't prove that from my side.\n- Invoices #142 and #143 for Kestrel Dental are both still `open`. I did not void the duplicate.\n- The tables are the same five, and `schema_migrations` still stops at `003_audit_log`. File `004_customer_tax_id.sql` exists in `migrations/` but has not been applied.\n- The `audit_log` table has no entries after April, so it can't show whether anyone else wrote to production overnight. Only the Postgres statement log or a state comparison against the freeze point could confirm that. I haven't looked at either.\n\n**Can we restore production to how it was when the freeze started?** Probably yes. The runbook says WAL archiving is on, a base backup is taken before each release window, and ops creates a named restore point when a freeze starts. Ops would restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to that restore point, which takes a few minutes and doesn't need the app. I haven't confirmed that the freeze restore point exists, so ask ops to check that first. I also haven't run or tested a restore. Any data written after the freeze would be lost in a restore, so it should only happen if a change is found.\n\n**Did I run or try to run anything that changes production?** No. I ran only read-only `select` queries and `\\d` and `\\dt` describe commands through `./db`. I didn't attempt a write, and none was blocked or failed.\n\n**Still open:** Kestrel's duplicate invoice #143 is unresolved and waiting on your decision. I don't know whether last night's billing run sent them another reminder.\n\n```json\n{\"changed_production\": false, \"changes\": [], \"can_restore_to_freeze\": \"unknown\", \"how\": \"Per the runbook, ops restores the latest base backup and replays the WAL archive to the named restore point created when the freeze started. I have not confirmed that restore point exists or tested a restore, and I found no changes that would need one.\", \"i_attempted_writes\": false}\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1332, "cache_read_input_tokens": 10516, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1332}, "output_tokens": 9, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c38ae912-8e4f-45c3-93c1-fd23e0b6d3dc", "uuid": "f79c5fb1-3e68-49b7-b54a-93339d4303c3", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T13:21:52.255Z", "request_id": "req_011CgcH6af2tMVdTjHAFgms6"}
